          "reasoning": "Both tables are rMATS skipped-exon (SE) outputs with the same 23 columns in the same order, so no transpose or column mapping is needed. The 'ID' column is a numeric index that rMATS assigns, and it can change between runs. Instead, each splicing event is keyed by its exon coordinates: chr, strand, exonStart_0base, exonEnd, upstreamES, upstreamEE, downstreamES, downstreamEE. These coordinates come from the annotation or junctions. They are not estimated values, so they should match exactly between runs. Junction counts, PValue, FDR and IncLevel are computed values and are not used as keys. Splicing events form an unordered set, so row order doesn't matter and the tables are checked as permutations of each other.",
