          "overall_reasoning": "This is the rMATS output for skipped-exon events, joined on the exon coordinate ID columns. There is only one row, so Pearson and Spearman correlation would be undefined. I used cell-by-cell relative absolute error (RAE) for every numerical column instead.\n\n- **Junction counts and form lengths:** IJC/SJC and IncFormLen/SkipFormLen are deterministic integers from read counting. They get a tight tolerance of 0.01.\n- **PValue and FDR:** rMATS computes these by numerical optimisation, so they can drift slightly between versions or runs. They get a moderate tolerance of 0.05.\n- **Inclusion levels (IncLevel1, IncLevel2):** These are ratios rounded to 3 decimals, so they get a tolerance of 0.05.\n- **IncLevelDifference:** The value is small (-0.023), so a 0.001 rounding difference alone gives an RAE of about 4%. Its tolerance is a looser 0.1. The sign is kept because it shows the direction of the effect.\n- **Gene annotation (GeneID, geneSymbol):** Compared as exact strings.\n- **Ignored columns (ID, ID.1):** These are arbitrary event indices that depend on the run.",
